sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (agreed with Nick, 2026-11-07): a slot is only a fixed identity that the Gateway keeps, `shark-tvm-3`: its Node record, WireGuard key and hub peer, SSH host key and agent secret. No slot VM waits; each task start makes a VM from the host's image and writes this identity onto it (docs/cli/tasks/provision.mmd), and a release deletes that VM (docs/cli/tasks/cancel.mmd).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · enrol one slot identity
  %% kind: task_vm.slot_enrol
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane HUB icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant HUB as VPN hub<br/>over ssh
  Note over GW: Make the identity<br/>once per slot number
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - the `slots` count of a task VM host (`node:update`): one enrol per missing identity, one at a time
  %%> - an identity whose enrol failed; one that still holds a model key after a failed release is released first
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Node `shark-tvm-3` with its `app-dev` role, its WireGuard address and its `pi-server` Process
  %%> - the identity's WireGuard key, SSH host key and agent secret, made by the Gateway and kept encrypted on the slot's row
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-slot-enrol
  SW->>HUB: Add the hub peer<br/>peer file · wg addconf
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the identity's peer file from its fixed public key and loads it; a rerun writes the same file
  %%> - a task start or a release never touches the hub
  alt the run passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Record the identity free<br/>Node active
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the identity is `failed` and no task start takes it; the slot rule enrols it again
  end
